<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<!--
	Tree demo: what a tree node answers to a gesture, and how the tree follows the model it shows.
	
	The tree is rooted at the ProjectScope type and shows its instances, their milestones and the
	tickets of each milestone.
	
	A click selects a node and writes it to the "selected" channel. A double-click - or Enter on
	the node carrying the keyboard cursor - activates it: the node becomes the selection and the
	tree's <on-activate> command runs with it, here writing it to the "activated" channel. Both
	channels are displayed below the tree, so selecting and opening a node are visibly different
	things.
	
	The tree selects any number of nodes. A plain click replaces the selection, a click with Ctrl
	adds a node to it or takes it out again, and a click with Shift selects the range from the node
	the selection started at. The keyboard works the same way: the up and down arrows, Home and End
	move the keyboard cursor alone and leave the selection where it is, Space adds the node the
	cursor is on to the selection or takes it out again, and an arrow with Shift grows the range
	from the node the selection started at. The right and left arrows expand and collapse the
	cursor node, stepping to its first child and back to its parent.
	
	The "selected" channel holds the selected node while exactly one is selected, the set of the
	selected nodes while there are several - displayed as their labels one after the other - and
	nothing while there is none. An activation names one node, so the "activated" channel always
	holds the single node the gesture opened.
	
	The tree follows the objects it displays. The "parents" expression says what holds an object in
	the tree - the milestone of a ticket, the scope of a milestone, the type the tree is built from
	for a scope. An object of one of the observed-types that is created or changed while the tree
	has no node for it is placed through "parents": the child list of the node holding it is
	brought up to date, so the object appears under its open holder, and the subtrees the user
	opened stay open. The node of an object written to "selected" is found the same way, by walking
	up from it instead of searching the whole tree.
	
	The five commands below show that in the five shapes a model change takes; a sixth one,
	"Approve", approves all selected milestones at once, see its comment:
	- "New milestone" creates a milestone in the selected scope through a dialog and writes it to
	"selected". The tree has no node for it while the dialog closes, and reveals and selects it
	as soon as the create arrives.
	- "New ticket" creates a ticket in the selected milestone without a dialog and writes it to
	"selected", so the node appears under the still-open milestone and is selected.
	- "Detach from milestone" takes the milestone off the selected ticket. Nothing is deleted, yet
	the ticket leaves the child list it hung in: its node goes, the milestone stays open and
	becomes the selection in its place.
	- "Attach a free ticket" gives a ticket without a milestone - a detached one, for instance - the
	selected milestone and writes it to "selected". The tree has no node for that ticket; the
	change places it under the still-open milestone, where it is selected.
	- "Delete" deletes whatever is selected, one object or several; where nothing of the selection
	is left, the node the first deleted object hung in becomes the selection.
	
	A command works on the selection through a derived channel naming what it can process: the
	selection while it is a single object, and that object while it is a scope, a milestone or a
	ticket. With <null-input-disabled/> that is the whole of "enabled for such a selection".
	
	On top of that, the model access rights of the user decide: <create-transient> and
	<delete-object> bring the rule for the creation and the deletion they perform, and the command
	running the script creating a ticket declares the creation in its <access>: a ticket created
	in the scope of the milestone and added to its tickets.
	
	The same objects are displayed twice, in the tabs "Tree" and "Tree table": a <tree-table> with
	the root, children and parents of the tree and with the name, due date and approval as columns.
	Both bind the "selected" channel, so the commands work on the selection of either, and an object
	written to it is revealed in both - the rows above it are opened, it is selected and scrolled
	into view, as the new ticket under a closed milestone of the tree table is. The display in the
	tab not shown follows the model as well: a name or due date changed in the details form beside
	the tabs, while the tree table is in the hidden tab, shows in its columns as soon as the tab is
	opened again, and when its selected object is deleted meanwhile, the row it hung in is selected.
	
	The details form edits the single selected object: the name, due date and approval of a
	milestone, the title of a ticket, the name of a scope.
-->
<view>
	<channels>
		<channel name="selected"/>
		<channel name="activated"/>
		<!--
			The selection while it consists of exactly one object, and nothing while nothing or
			several objects are selected: size() counts a missing value as zero, a single object as
			one and a set as the number of its elements.
		-->
		<derived-channel name="selectedSingle"
			expr="if($selected.size() == 1, $selected.singleElement(), null)"
			inputs="selected"
		/>
		<!-- The single selection while it is a scope, a milestone, a ticket - nothing otherwise. -->
		<derived-channel name="selectedScope"
			expr="if($selectedSingle.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`), $selectedSingle, null)"
			inputs="selectedSingle"
		/>
		<derived-channel name="selectedMilestone"
			expr="if($selectedSingle.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`), $selectedSingle, null)"
			inputs="selectedSingle"
		/>
		<derived-channel name="selectedTicket"
			expr="if($selectedSingle.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket`), $selectedSingle, null)"
			inputs="selectedSingle"
		/>
		<!-- The selected milestones while the selection consists of milestones only, of any projects. -->
		<derived-channel name="selectedMilestones"
			expr="{ milestones = $selected.filter(n -> $n.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`)); if(!$milestones.isEmpty() &amp;&amp; $milestones.size() == $selected.size(), $milestones, null); }"
			inputs="selected"
		/>
	</channels>
	<split-panel
		orientation="horizontal"
		resizable="true"
	>
		<panes>
			<pane
				size="60"
				unit="%"
			>
				<panel>
					<title>
						<en>Tree Demo</en>
						<de>Baum-Demo</de>
					</title>
					<commands>
						<generic-command
							image="css:bi bi-plus-lg"
							inputs="selectedScope"
							placement="TOOLBAR"
						>
							<label>
								<en>New milestone</en>
								<de>Neuer Meilenstein</de>
							</label>
							<executability>
								<null-input-disabled/>
							</executability>
							<create-transient
								container="selectedScope"
								reference="milestones"
								type="tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone"
							>
								<with-result>
									<open-dialog
										bind-input-to="model"
										dialog-view="demo/create-milestone.view.xml"
									>
										<bind
											channel="container"
											to="selectedScope"
										/>
										<bind
											channel="selection"
											to="selected"
										/>
									</open-dialog>
								</with-result>
							</create-transient>
						</generic-command>
						<!--
							The ticket is created without a dialog, so the script gets the milestone as the
							command's input. The ticket is created in the context of its scope, which numbers the
							tickets of a project continuously. A ticket hangs in the scope's composition and names
							its milestone; the milestone's ticket list is the backwards side of that reference and
							is not written to.
						-->
						<generic-command
							image="css:bi bi-ticket-perforated"
							inputs="selectedMilestone as milestone"
							placement="TOOLBAR"
						>
							<label>
								<en>New ticket</en>
								<de>Neues Ticket</de>
							</label>
							<access>
								<create
									in="$milestone.container()"
									reference="tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope#tickets"
								/>
							</access>
							<executability>
								<null-input-disabled/>
							</executability>
							<with-transaction>
								<commitMessage>
									<en>Created a ticket in milestone {0}.</en>
									<de>Ticket in Meilenstein {0} angelegt.</de>
								</commitMessage>
								<execute-script function="{ scope = $milestone.container(); ticket = new(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket`, context: $scope, transient: false); $ticket.set(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket#title`, 'Ticket ' + ($scope.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope#tickets`).size() + 1)); $scope.add(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope#tickets`, $ticket); $ticket.set(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket#milestone`, $milestone); $ticket; }"/>
								<with-result>
									<write-channel name="selected"/>
								</with-result>
							</with-transaction>
						</generic-command>
						<generic-command
							image="css:bi bi-box-arrow-up"
							inputs="selectedTicket as ticket"
							placement="TOOLBAR"
						>
							<label>
								<en>Detach from milestone</en>
								<de>Von Meilenstein lösen</de>
							</label>
							<executability>
								<null-input-disabled/>
							</executability>
							<with-transaction>
								<execute-script function="{ $ticket.set(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket#milestone`, null); null; }"/>
							</with-transaction>
						</generic-command>
						<!--
							A ticket without a milestone hangs in no child list of the tree. The command attaches
							the first such ticket of the selected milestone's scope to the milestone and writes it
							to "selected". The tickets are observed, because whether there is a free ticket depends
							on objects beyond the selected milestone. Should the free ticket be gone by the time the
							command runs, the script answers the milestone, which leaves the selection where it is.
						-->
						<generic-command
							image="css:bi bi-box-arrow-in-down"
							inputs="selectedMilestone as milestone"
							observed-types="tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket"
							placement="TOOLBAR"
						>
							<label>
								<en>Attach a free ticket</en>
								<de>Freies Ticket anhängen</de>
							</label>
							<executability>
								<null-input-disabled/>
								<disabled-if expr="if($milestone.container().get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope#tickets`).filter(t -> $t.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket#milestone`) == null).isEmpty(), #('The project has no ticket without a milestone.'@en, 'Das Projekt hat kein Ticket ohne Meilenstein.'@de), null)"/>
							</executability>
							<with-transaction>
								<commitMessage>
									<en>Attached a ticket to milestone {0}.</en>
									<de>Ticket an Meilenstein {0} angehängt.</de>
								</commitMessage>
								<execute-script function="{ ticket = $milestone.container().get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope#tickets`).filter(t -> $t.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket#milestone`) == null).firstElement(); if($ticket == null, $milestone, { $ticket.set(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket#milestone`, $milestone); $ticket; }); }"/>
								<with-result>
									<write-channel name="selected"/>
								</with-result>
							</with-transaction>
						</generic-command>
						<!--
							Approves all selected milestones, which may belong to different projects. The access
							requires the operation "Approve" on the project of every selected milestone, the check
							the privileged script approveMilestones makes as well: a selection reaching into a
							project the user may not approve in disables the command and names the refusal.
						-->
						<generic-command
							image="css:bi bi-patch-check"
							inputs="selectedMilestones as milestones"
							placement="TOOLBAR"
						>
							<label>
								<en>Approve</en>
								<de>Freigeben</de>
							</label>
							<access>
								<operation name="Approve"
									object="$milestones.map(m -> $m.container())"
									type="tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope"
								/>
							</access>
							<executability>
								<null-input-disabled/>
							</executability>
							<with-transaction>
								<execute-script function="approveMilestones($milestones)"/>
							</with-transaction>
						</generic-command>
						<!-- <delete-object/> deletes a single object as well as a set of them. -->
						<generic-command
							image="css:bi bi-trash"
							inputs="selected"
							placement="TOOLBAR"
						>
							<label>
								<en>Delete</en>
								<de>Löschen</de>
							</label>
							<executability>
								<null-input-disabled/>
							</executability>
							<delete-object/>
						</generic-command>
					</commands>
					<tab-bar active-tab="tree">
						<tabs>
							<tab id="tree"
								icon="css:bi bi-diagram-2"
							>
								<label>
									<en>Tree</en>
									<de>Baum</de>
								</label>
								<tree
									observed-types="tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope,tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone,tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket"
									selection="selected"
									selection-mode="multi"
								>
									<root>`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`</root>
									<children>if($node == `tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`, all(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`), if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`), $node.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope#milestones`), if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`), $node.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone#tickets`), [])))</children>
									<parents>if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket`), $node.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket#milestone`), if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`), $node.container(), if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`), `tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`, null)))</parents>
									<on-activate class="com.top_logic.layout.view.command.GenericViewCommand">
										<write-channel name="activated"/>
									</on-activate>
								</tree>
							</tab>
							<tab id="tree-table"
								icon="css:bi bi-list-nested"
							>
								<label>
									<en>Tree table</en>
									<de>Baumtabelle</de>
								</label>
								<tree-table
									observed-types="tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope,tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone,tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket"
									personalization-key="tree-demo-tree-table"
									selection="selected"
									selection-mode="multi"
								>
									<root>`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`</root>
									<children>if($node == `tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`, all(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`), if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`), $node.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope#milestones`), if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`), $node.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone#tickets`), [])))</children>
									<parents>if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket`), $node.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket#milestone`), if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`), $node.container(), if($node.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`), `tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`, null)))</parents>
									<columns>
										<computed-column name="name"
											type="tl.core:String"
										>
											<label>
												<en>Name</en>
												<de>Name</de>
											</label>
											<value><![CDATA[if($row.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket`), $row.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket#title`), if($row.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`), $row.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone#name`), $row.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope#name`)))]]></value>
										</computed-column>
										<computed-column name="dueDate"
											type="tl.core:Date"
										>
											<label>
												<en>Due date</en>
												<de>Fälligkeitsdatum</de>
											</label>
											<value><![CDATA[if($row.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`), $row.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone#dueDate`), null)]]></value>
										</computed-column>
										<computed-column name="approved"
											type="tl.core:Boolean"
										>
											<label>
												<en>Approved</en>
												<de>Genehmigt</de>
											</label>
											<value><![CDATA[if($row.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`), $row.get(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone#approved`), null)]]></value>
										</computed-column>
									</columns>
									<on-activate class="com.top_logic.layout.view.command.GenericViewCommand">
										<write-channel name="activated"/>
									</on-activate>
								</tree-table>
							</tab>
						</tabs>
					</tab-bar>
					<inset>
						<text>
							<label>
								<en>Selected node</en>
								<de>Ausgewählter Knoten</de>
							</label>
						</text>
						<text input="selected"/>
						<text>
							<label>
								<en>Activated node</en>
								<de>Aktivierter Knoten</de>
							</label>
						</text>
						<text input="activated"/>
					</inset>
				</panel>
			</pane>
			<pane
				size="40"
				unit="%"
			>
				<panel>
					<title>
						<en>Details</en>
						<de>Details</de>
					</title>
					<switch input="selectedSingle as object">
						<case test="$object.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Milestone`)">
							<form
								input="selectedMilestone"
								with-inset="true"
								withEditMode="true"
							>
								<field attribute="name"/>
								<field attribute="dueDate"/>
								<field attribute="approved"/>
							</form>
						</case>
						<case test="$object.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:Ticket`)">
							<form
								input="selectedTicket"
								with-inset="true"
								withEditMode="true"
							>
								<field attribute="title"/>
							</form>
						</case>
						<case test="$object.instanceOf(`tl.demo.projectManagement:ProjectScope`)">
							<form
								input="selectedScope"
								with-inset="true"
								withEditMode="true"
							>
								<field attribute="name"/>
							</form>
						</case>
						<default>
							<inset>
								<text>
									<label>
										<en>Select a single node to edit it.</en>
										<de>Einen einzelnen Knoten auswählen, um ihn zu bearbeiten.</de>
									</label>
								</text>
							</inset>
						</default>
					</switch>
				</panel>
			</pane>
		</panes>
	</split-panel>
</view>